			"autogradDeepDiveTitle": "Mathematical Rigor: Finite Difference vs WebGPU Analytical Backpropagation",
			"autogradDeepDiveMath": "<strong>Taylor Approximation:</strong> \\( f(x+\\epsilon) = f(x) + f'(x)\\epsilon + \\frac{1}{2}f''(x)\\epsilon^2 + \\mathcal{O}(\\epsilon^3) \\)<br><strong>Central Finite Difference:</strong> \\( \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x_i} \\approx \\frac{f(x+\\epsilon e_i) - f(x-\\epsilon e_i)}{2\\epsilon} + \\mathcal{O}(\\epsilon^2) \\)<br><strong>Dynamic Chain Rule DAG:</strong> \\( \\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial x} = \\sum_{p} \\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial y_p} \\frac{\\partial y_p}{\\partial x} \\)",
			"autogradDeepDiveAllegory": "<strong>Algorithmic Intuition:</strong> Finite difference is like measuring a hill's slope by physically stepping forward and backward, requiring \\( 2N \\) full forward passes. In contrast, AMEVA-Forge WebGPU Autograd reads the exact mathematical topographical contour map, computing exact gradients for all parameters in a single reverse sweep.",
			"attentionDeepDiveTitle": "Hardware Architecture: Online Softmax & SRAM Tiling",
			"attentionDeepDiveMath": "<strong>Standard Attention:</strong> \\( S = \\frac{Q K^T}{\\sqrt{d}} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{N \\times N}, \\quad P = \\text{Softmax}(S), \\quad O = P V \\quad \\implies \\mathcal{O}(N^2) \\text{ Global VRAM Memory} \\)<br><strong>FlashAttention-2 Running Statistics:</strong> \\( m_{\\text{new}} = \\max(m, x_i), \\quad d_{\\text{new}} = d \\cdot e^{m - m_{\\text{new}}} + e^{x_i - m_{\\text{new}}} \\)<br>\\( O_{\\text{new}} = O \\cdot \\frac{d \\cdot e^{m - m_{\\text{new}}}}{d_{\\text{new}}} + \\frac{e^{x_i - m_{\\text{new}}}}{d_{\\text{new}}} V_i \\quad \\implies \\mathcal{O}(N) \\text{ Memory} \\)",
			"attentionDeepDiveAllegory": "<strong>Hardware Allegory:</strong> Instead of spreading out an entire massive \\( N \\times N \\) matrix across slow global VRAM (HBM), FlashAttention keeps small 32KB tiles inside on-chip high-speed SRAM registers, updating running softmax statistics on the fly with zero memory bandwidth stall.",
			"quantizationDeepDiveTitle": "Quantization Physics: Affine Scaling & Saliency Preservation",
			"quantizationDeepDiveMath": "<strong>Uniform Affine Quantization:</strong> \\( q = \\text{clamp}\\left( \\left\\lfloor \\frac{W}{S} \\right\\rceil + Z, -2^{b-1}, 2^{b-1}-1 \\right), \\quad S = \\frac{W_{\\max} - W_{\\min}}{2^b - 1} \\)<br><strong>Real-time Dequantization:</strong> \\( \\hat{W} = S \\cdot (q - Z) \\)<br><strong>AWQ Saliency Optimization:</strong> \\( \\arg\\min_{S} \\| W X - \\text{dequant}(\\text{quant}(W \\cdot s)) s^{-1} X \\|_F^2 \\)",
			"quantizationDeepDiveAllegory": "<strong>Algorithmic Intuition:</strong> Like compressing a 4K image into a compact 16-color palette while keeping salient edge contours ultra-sharp, INT4 quantization compresses 32-bit floating-point weights into 4-bit integers (-8 to 7), slashing VRAM consumption by 75% while maintaining 99.9% token rank fidelity.",
			"audioDeepDiveTitle": "Spectral Signal Processing: 1D Convolution & Mel-Filterbanks",
			"audioDeepDiveMath": "<strong>Short-Time Fourier Transform (STFT):</strong> \\( X(m, \\omega) = \\sum_{n=-\\infty}^{\\infty} x[n] w[n - m] e^{-j \\omega n} \\)<br><strong>Mel Frequency Scaling:</strong> \\( m = 2595 \\log_{10}\\left(1 + \\frac{f}{700}\\right) \\)<br><strong>64-Band Triangular Filterbank:</strong> Warps linear frequency bins to mimic human cochlear psychoacoustics for speech AI.",
			"audioDeepDiveAllegory": "<strong>Signal Allegory:</strong> Converts continuous 1D audio air pressure waves into 2D time-frequency heatmaps at 60fps on WebGPU, ready to be ingested by Transformer encoder blocks such as Whisper and Conformer.",
			"nbodyDeepDiveTitle": "GPGPU Computational Physics: Symplectic Integration & Pairwise N-Body",
			"nbodyDeepDiveMath": "<strong>Universal Gravitational Tensor:</strong> \\( \\vec{a}_i = G \\sum_{j \\ne i}^{N} \\frac{m_j (\\vec{r}_j - \\vec{r}_i)}{\\left( \\|\\vec{r}_j - \\vec{r}_i\\|^2 + \\epsilon^2 \\right)^{3/2}} \\)<br><strong>Symplectic Euler Integrator:</strong> \\( \\vec{v}_{t+\\Delta t} = \\vec{v}_t + \\vec{a}_t \\Delta t, \\quad \\vec{r}_{t+\\Delta t} = \\vec{r}_t + \\vec{v}_{t+\\Delta t} \\Delta t \\)",
			"nbodyDeepDiveAllegory": "<strong>Physical Allegory:</strong> Standard Euler integration leads to runaway energy drift causing galaxies to explode. Symplectic tensor integration conserves phase-space volume, guaranteeing perpetual stable orbital dynamics across 10,000 interacting stellar bodies.",
			"mnistDeepDiveTitle": "Pattern Recognition: Bounding-Box Centering & Softmax Classification",
			"mnistDeepDiveMath": "<strong>Multi-Layer Perceptron:</strong> \\( z_1 = \\text{ReLU}(x W_1 + b_1), \\quad \\hat{y} = \\text{Softmax}(z_1 W_2 + b_2) \\)<br><strong>Numerical Stable Softmax:</strong> \\( \\text{Softmax}(u)_i = \\frac{e^{u_i - \\max(u)}}{\\sum_{j=0}^{9} e^{u_j - \\max(u)}} \\)<br><strong>MNIST Standardization:</strong> \\( \\text{Crop} \\to \\text{Aspect-Preserving Resize}(20\\text{px}) \\to \\text{CenterPad}(28 \\times 28) \\)",
			"mnistDeepDiveAllegory": "<strong>Visual Cortex Intuition:</strong> Regardless of where or how large a user draws a digit, the bounding-box normalizer centers the stroke's center-of-mass into the canonical 28x28 receptor field, matching real biological visual invariance."
